   263	The proof does not apply Zariski–Nagata purity to Orevkov's merely continuous
   264	collapsed map `f*`.  It applies it to the promoted finite flat morphism
   265	`q:Y->C^2`, with `Y` normal and the target regular.  Codimension-one points
   266	of `Y` in `U` are unramified by Keller, while a boundary prime is generically
   267	ramified exactly when its `mu_l>=2`.  If every dicritical is trivial, `q` is
   268	unramified in codimension one; purity rules out a branch locus supported at
   269	only the correction points.  Hence `q` is finite etale.  Since `Y` is
   270	irreducible and `C^2` has no nontrivial connected finite etale cover, its
   271	degree would be one.  The correction jumps of `f*` do not invalidate this
   272	argument; rather, purity shows that such isolated jumps cannot occur without
   273	a ramified boundary divisor in the finite model.
