The source map has exposed one material publication/preprint divergence: the Russian paper retains “outside a finite set” in the \(\mu=1\) sentence, while the English aid drops it. I’m treating the Russian wording as authoritative and still checking the \(\mu=2\) proof independently. The first local repair found inside that track is a miscitation in Lemma 13: its equality comes from the rooted-branch lemma, not the positivity lemma.
